{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Seeing.</b> A strange word, on account of the combination of two patterns of the infinitive construct; the familiar form and its parallel occur. Likewise: they see many things but do not guard them — the soul or the eye; and his ears are open but do not close them, and do not hear. And this is astonishing."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:36.694185991Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}